# Batch: 2026-Q3-logdef-infectious-01
# Pattern: logical_definition_import v2.0.0
# Generated: 2026-07-28T09:15:00Z (revised 2026-08-02)
# Attributed to: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0295-7821 (Samson Tu)
# Scope: Foundation infectious disease entities lacking logical definitions
# Total: 152 logical definitions (143 ready + 9 deferred)
#
# REVISION NOTE (2026-08-02):
#   - All definitions derive from Mondo EquivalentClasses axioms
#   - No constructed definitions; 4 diseases without Mondo EquivalentClasses excluded
#     (typhoid fever, malaria, rabies, visceral leishmaniasis)
#   - Filler classes reference ICD extension codes by WHO-FIC Foundation entity IRI
#     (from whofic-2025-05-24-labeled.owl)
#   - Extension codes are descendants of ICD Extension Code
#     (http://id.who.int/icd/entity/1920852714)
#   - Each axiom carries skos:closeMatch annotations recording the original
#     NCBITaxon/UBERON IRIs for cross-ontology interoperability
#
# AUDIT NOTE (2026-08-02):
#   - WHO-FIC audit found 19 of 28 "proposed" extension codes already exist
#     in whofic-2025-05-24-labeled.owl (see qc/whofic_audit.tsv)
#   - Only 9 codes truly need proposal (5 infectious agents + 4 anatomy)
#   - 18 formerly-deferred definitions reclassified as READY
#   - HermiT reasoner: PASS (0 inconsistent, 0 unsatisfiable classes)
#
# Definitions are partitioned into:
#   READY (143): All fillers are existing ICD extension code entities in WHO-FIC
#   DEFERRED (9): One or more fillers require proposed new extension codes
#                 from batch 2026-Q3-extcode-infectious-01
#                 (Leishmania braziliensis, Balamuthia mandrillaris,
#                  Human enterovirus 71, Nipah virus, Hendra virus,
#                  Intestinal mucosa, Biliary system, Portal venous system,
#                  Lymphoid tissue)

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PART 1: READY LOGICAL DEFINITIONS (143)
# All filler classes are existing ICD extension code entities.
# Entity IRIs: http://id.who.int/icd/entity/<id>
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# LDEF-001: Cholera ≡ Certain infectious or parasitic diseases
#   AND infectiousAgent some Vibrio cholerae (http://id.who.int/icd/entity/824826401)
# Mondo source: MONDO:0015766 cholera
#   EquivClass: infectious disease AND has_infectious_agent some NCBITaxon:666
EquivalentClasses(
  Annotation(prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0015766>)
  Annotation(dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>)
  Annotation(dct:rightsHolder "Mondo Disease Ontology Consortium")
  Annotation(dct:source <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0015766>)
  Annotation(icd:batchId "2026-Q3-logdef-infectious-01")
  Annotation(icd:definitionStatus "ready")
  Annotation(skos:closeMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_666>)
  <http://id.who.int/icd/entity/257068234>
  ObjectIntersectionOf(
    <http://id.who.int/icd/entity/1435254666>
    ObjectSomeValuesFrom(icd:infectiousAgent <http://id.who.int/icd/entity/824826401>)
  )
)

